{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 89, :comments ["<b>And when Moses entered the Tent of Meeting to speak with Him, he heard the voice.</b> And though this matter was very slight in comparison to the dedication of Solomon's Temple, nevertheless whenever Moses entered the Tent of Meeting he would hear that same voice he had heard before the incident of the Golden Calf — and this did not occur in the First Temple, all the more so in the Second Temple, for no prophet went to the Sanctuary to prophesy so as to attain prophecy immediately. This was because this dedication and its offerers and Moses, who was their shepherd, were acceptable.</p>" "<b>Speaking.</b> Between Him and Himself, for כָּל פָּעַל ה׳ לְמַעֲנֵהוּ (Proverbs 16:4). By contemplating Himself He thereby knows and confers good upon others through the bounty of overflow that admits no limitation, and the effect appears in the recipient according to his disposition. In this manner he explained the mode of every act of speaking mentioned in the Torah with the expression וַיְדַבֵּר ה׳."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:09.573222888Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}